---

<section class="py-12 bg-gray-50">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-center mb-2">THE NEUKWI NËU & SILVER JUBILEE</h1>
    <h2 class="text-xl text-center text-gray-600 mb-8">Fo’o NGWADEZA III | Theme: STEWARDSHIP & VISION</h2>
    
    <div class="space-y-6">
      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Friday December 4th — Mametah (Day 0)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Village Cleansing</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li>The entire village will drop Atetoh at the palace square. After 7 days, it will be used for village purification.</li>
          <li>Kwihfo in all-night communication with the Ancestors.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Saturday December 12th — Mametah (Day 1)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Opening & Cultural Cleansing (The Awakening)</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>6:00 AM:</strong> Campfire in replacement of gunshots across the seven hills of Nsongwa announcing the dawn of the jubilee.</li>
          <li><strong>7:00 AM:</strong> Sacred cleansing and purification rites by the Fon and Kwihfo at the palace shrines (Tap Tap).</li>
          <li><strong>8:00 AM:</strong> Arrival of the population and Dignitaries (Religious, traditional authorities, political parties, RDAC, Bamenda administrative/municipal authorities, Courts, Parliament, City Mayor, SDO Mezam, Brigadier General, Vice Chancellor, Public Independent Conciliator, Regional Assembly delegation).</li>
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Arrival of the Governor of the North West Region / Minister of Arts and Culture / MINAT.</li>
          <li><strong>11:00 AM:</strong> Royal Procession led by Lerère, National and Nsongwa Anthems, Ecumenical Prayer, Welcome by Prince Nathan Asanji, and Cutting of the Silver Jubilee Cake.</li>
          <li><strong>Speeches:</strong> NTC Chairman, HRM Fo’o Ngwadeza III, President of House of Chiefs, Governor/Minister, Awards, Twin & Fumben Dances.</li>
          <li><strong>3:00 PM:</strong> Magazine/Museum Launch by the Mayor of BCC / Mayor of Bamenda II, followed by Cameroonian Artists' Musical Entertainment.</li>
          <li><strong>6:00 PM:</strong> Traditional campfire lighting and evening storytelling sessions (Njallah) with village elders.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Sunday December 13th — Yidzong (Day 3)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Ecumenical Day (Prayers for Peace & Unity)</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>09:00 AM:</strong> Joint inter-denominational prayers for the health of HRM Fo’o Ngwadeza III & the safety of the village.</li>
          <li><strong>12:00 PM:</strong> Choral music competition featuring local, regional, and church choirs.</li>
          <li><strong>03:00 PM:</strong> Royal charity visit: Thanksgiving and food supplies for underprivileged and displaced families within the subdivision.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Monday December 14th — Yakab (Day 4)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Education & Youth Empowerment Day</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>09:00 AM:</strong> Inter-school cultural quizzes, debates, and an essay competition focused on Ngemba history and language preservation.</li>
          <li><strong>03:00 PM:</strong> Handover of school supplies, academic scholarships, and prizes by the NDECA Education Committee.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Tuesday December 15th — Mbieg’ndoung (Day 5)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Health Wellness Drive</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>08:00 AM:</strong> Free medical screening campaign at the Nsongwa Palace (consultations, eye tests, blood pressure, diabetic screening) coordinated by the Mary Alieh Foundation.</li>
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Public health sensitization seminar on preventive medicine, hygiene, and clean water by Bamenda Regional Hospital in partnership with Mary Alieh Foundation.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Wednesday December 16th — Yinkoung (Day 6)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Sports, Health & Traditional Wrestling</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>08:00 AM:</strong> Conclude free medical screening and distribute prescribed medications.</li>
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Traditional wrestling matches and tug-of-war between youths of neighboring quarters.</li>
          <li><strong>02:00 PM:</strong> Kick-Off, Fo’o Ngwadeza III Silver Jubilee Football Tournament (Semi-Finals Matches).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Thursday December 17th — San’neh (Day 7)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Women Empowerment & Culinary Arts Day</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>09:00 AM:</strong> General Assembly of all Nsongwa Women’s Cultural groups, Mothers’ Union, Dance Groups, Age groups (Nkang), etc.</li>
          <li><strong>11:00 AM:</strong> Traditional culinary competition: Live exhibition of authentic Ngeumba dishes (Achu, yellow soup, black soup, Akwa).</li>
          <li><strong>02:00 PM:</strong> Seminar on micro-trade, financial literacy, and Cooperative/Bank management hosted by Credit Unions and Banks.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Friday December 18th — Mbig’neh (Day 8)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Arts, Craft & Museum Launching</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>09:00 AM:</strong> Exhibition of Nsongwa traditional wood carvings, Royal garments, pottery, and beadwork.</li>
          <li><strong>11:30 AM:</strong> Symposium: “Preserving the Nsongwa-Ngemba identity in a Digital World.”</li>
          <li><strong>02:00 PM:</strong> NEUKWI RITES.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Saturday December 19th — Yinkaheh (Day 9)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Diaspora Homecoming & Welcoming Rites</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Arrival and welcoming ceremony for Nsongwa elites returning from the USA, Europe, South Africa, UAE, and national cities.</li>
          <li><strong>01:00 PM:</strong> Interactive town hall session: Diaspora investment for infrastructure and sustainable development in Nsongwa.</li>
          <li><strong>07:00 PM:</strong> Traditional night: Evening reception and dinner hosted by the Palace for all home-comers.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Sunday December 20th — Mametah (Day 10)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">Sports Finals & Corporate Activation Day</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Corporate exhibition hours, activation, and promotion by headline partners (MTN, UBA, Orange, Ecobank, UCB, Boissons du Cameroun, Camtel, UBC, Credit Unions, etc.).</li>
          <li><strong>03:00 PM:</strong> Grand Finale of the Fo’o Ngwadeza III Silver Jubilee Football Tournament.</li>
          <li><strong>05:30 PM:</strong> Trophy presentation and corporate networking evening.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Monday December 21st — Yidzong (Day 11)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">General Assembly & Developmental Blueprint</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>09:00 AM:</strong> NDECA Annual General Assembly: Review of community achievements and evaluation of Infrastructure Projects.</li>
          <li><strong>12:00 PM:</strong> Traditional Decorations/Recognitions.</li>
          <li><strong>01:00 PM:</strong> Launch of Nsongwa 2027/2028 Vision (Focusing on clean water, expansion of electricity, road networks).</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-md">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-700">Tuesday December 22nd — Yakab (Day 12)</h3>
        <p class="font-semibold text-gray-700">End of Neukwi - Convocation of Dignitaries & Visiting Fons</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside mt-2 text-gray-600 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>10:00 AM:</strong> Official arrival, reception, and protocol welcoming of visiting Fons from across the Northwest and Cameroon.</li>
          <li><strong>10:30 AM:</strong> Arrival of Administrative Officials.</li>
          <li><strong>11:00 AM:</strong> Royal solidarity parade and fraternal cultural exchanges between visiting traditional delegations.</li>
          <li><strong>1:00 PM:</strong> Private inner-palace royal banquet for visiting Fons and Administrative Officials.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
